  "_comment": "components maps each inlined component id to a short hash of the snippet it was built from. A differing hash means the library has moved on since this site was delivered - which is the question the care plan has to answer.",
  "is_demo": true,
  "_allow_past_dates_reason": "The case study's publication date. A case study about finished work is supposed to be in the past.",
  "allow_strings": {
    "hello@example.co.uk": "Deliberate. RFC 2606 reserves example.co.uk for exactly this, so the address cannot reach a real person. A plausible invented domain could belong to somebody. Replace with the real address on a client site, and with the demo's own domain the day this is deployed.",
    "example.co.uk": "Same as above - the domain half of the reserved fictional address.",
    "ph-photo": "Honest. This site has no photographs because the library ships none and will not use stock. The hero is a CSS stand-in at the true aspect ratio, so real pictures drop in without moving the layout. On a client site this must become a real <img> with width, height and loading.",
    "privacy@example.co.uk": "Deliberate. RFC 2606 reserves example.co.uk so it can never reach a real inbox, which is what you want on a demonstration site. Same reason as hello@example.co.uk above. On a real client this is a live address and somebody has to monitor it - a privacy notice naming an unmonitored inbox is worse than one naming the general one."
  },
